    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with a heavy focus on speed-leveraged production, prioritizing categorical volume in SB while navigating a difficult matchup against Nola. **Jorge Polanco** holds a marginal start grade of 53.87; while he sits lower in the order than we\u2019d prefer, the projected wind blowing out at the park provides a critical 5% boost to his raw power metrics, helping offset the skill of the opposing arm. We are operating with a significantly depleted core today, as **Kyle Tucker**, **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.**, and **Gunnar Henderson** are all inactive due to team off-days, and **Luis Robert Jr.** remains sidelined on the IL. Consequently, the reliance on high-upside prospects like **Jackson Merrill**, **Heliot Ramos**, and **Jordan Westburg** becomes paramount to maintain our pacing in Roto standings.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench involved **Coby Mayo** and **Miguel Vargas**, both of whom narrowly missed the cut behind **Jorge Polanco** due to projected defensive alignments and efficiency constraints. **Coby Mayo** represents the highest volatility bench piece, as his power profile is negated today by a high-efficiency opponent, making him a \"keep-fresh\" asset for tomorrow\u2019s more favorable splits. Meanwhile, the bottom of our roster\u2014including **Nasim Nunez**, **Cole Carrigg**, and **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.**\u2014will be monitored closely for late-inning pinch-running opportunities; in our league\u2019s landscape, the scarcity of stolen bases makes the late-game insertion of **Nasim Nunez** a primary tactical priority regardless of his total projected score. We are managing the roster cautiously, holding **Jacob Wilson**, **Drake Baldwin**, **Andy Pages**, and **Josh Jung** in reserve to ensure we do not hit our daily game cap prematurely in what looks like a volatile offensive environment.",
